WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:01.530
Prime Minister.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.760
Thank you so much for being here with us on
DW News.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.620
You've taken over Sudan at a historical moment.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.920
The country has is facing many challenges,
did you have any doubts about wanting to take

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.349
this role?

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:18.880
It's not really a personal wish.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.010
This is a wish that is responding to a call
of duty.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:31.380
So I did not have a single doubt in responding
to that, knowing so well, it is full of challenges,

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.920
it is dynamic, it is non-linear.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.489
You get it right today.

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:38.260
You have problems and hurdles tomorrow.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:49.039
Taking this job was a response to the calls
of the nation, my people who have managed

00:00:49.039 --> 00:01:00.179
to give the world one of the probably very
rare moments of change particularly in our

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:08.729
history something that we equate it to the
great moments in nations’ history, equal

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:17.780
to the fall of the Berlin Wall, years or centuries
back probably, the French Revolution.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:25.380
That momentous change created the environment
for me and many others to come, to help build

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.940
a news nation, it is a dawn.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:32.450
I was in Sudan back in April at the sit-in
front of the military headquarters and I saw

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.010
many young people.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:38.920
They were full of expectation and hope from
the government that eventually became your

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.920
government.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.420
Do you feel like your government is living
up to their expectations?

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:54.640
This is what make(s) us tick, the hope, the
expectations about us, about the change (from)

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.310
the government by our people.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.640
We never promised that we are willing to do
this on our own.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:09.750
It's a shared responsibility, we rise and
fall in this process together with one conviction

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.680
that we have two options either to succeed
or succeed.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.120
And I think we are moving in that direction.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.560
But a lot of young people that I've spoken
to in the past couple of days say the things

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:26.099
that they went to the streets for, like basic
living conditions including bread.

00:02:26.099 --> 00:02:27.430
These things have not been fulfilled.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.480
So do you think that the young people's expectations
were too high?

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.819
no their expectations were never too high.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:40.769
It is normal expectations by any government
by its people.

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:48.959
But also I'm sure they understand, they appreciate,
we inherited a daunting challenge a legacy

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:50.370
of 30 years.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:57.800
You cannot undo it overnight but I think equipped
with that conviction and determination with

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.209
our people working together.

00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:07.440
We had no doubts that we will be able to address
this and overcome these challenges.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:13.360
What do you tell the young people who perhaps
are feeling impatient with the delivery of

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.530
actual results to their lives?

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:20.480
One thing let us work together to address
these issues.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.780
Expectations are one thing, but let us address
these expectations together.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:32.129
Our interests are aligned we don't have different
interests from theirs, expectation is the

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:33.129
same.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:37.030
So let us join forces in addressing all this
challenges together.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:42.670
Sudan is being run now under a unique cooperation
between civilians and military.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:46.069
How is the cooperation between these two sides?

00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:48.689
Because it hasn't always been smooth has it?

00:03:48.689 --> 00:03:49.689
Yes.

00:03:49.689 --> 00:03:54.159
This is also another feature of the uniqueness
of this Sudanese experiment.

00:03:54.159 --> 00:04:03.040
We are proudly propagating this across the
world and calling it the Sudanese model which

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:11.719
is a partnership between the civilian and
the military, to build democracy with the

00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:13.950
solid foundation for democracy.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.090
This partnership is working.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.680
It is not free from challenges, there are
so many challenges.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:24.470
But I think there is a determination on both
sides to make it work and we are doing that

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.960
precisely.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:33.150
If you look at the region around us the failures
in many places, because I think they were

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:40.440
not able to establish an accord that would
allow such partnership to move the country

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.440
forward.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.110
We know we are experimenting with it.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:55.070
We know there is no transition that is smooth,
transitions are always messy non-linear and

00:04:55.070 --> 00:05:03.220
I think that in itself what makes it a very
interesting experiment to be a part of.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:07.550
Do you trust the military side of your government?

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:10.100
Do you trust them?

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:13.280
Absolutely, I do
Because some young people that I've spoken

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:20.210
to have said this military has been involved
in the oppression and at some point even the

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.040
killing of so many protesters.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.290
I do appreciate the views that expressed by
our young people.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:31.280
Remember these are young people who are subjected
to all kinds of oppression.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:36.800
You lived through that and you know it in
the streets and all this for years for decades.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:37.889
That's why they have these views.

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:41.900
But I think gradually we are building this
partnership together.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:48.690
None of this equation, these two sides of
the equation will be able to move on their

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:50.639
own to build this new nation.

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:57.070
I appreciate those views but we are working
together to address them.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:04.229
Let's turn to the topic of the clearing of
the sit in in June and the people that were

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:05.680
killed on the streets.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.699
A lot of them believe that the Rapid Support
Forces were involved in this attack.

00:06:10.699 --> 00:06:13.759
When will these people see justice?

00:06:13.759 --> 00:06:19.479
Because so far some say the results just have
not been up to what happened to protesters

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:20.479
on the streets.

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:23.220
I'm sure you know so well.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:32.349
The Constitutional document which is guiding
this transitional period has a very clear

00:06:32.349 --> 00:06:36.210
undertaking that we establish an investigation
committee.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:43.580
So let us not jump to conclusion, that investigation
committee formed from very respected lawyers

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:46.690
and people in the legal field in Sudan.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:52.760
They started their work over three months
now and they are doing their work and produce

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.020
the report.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:59.140
You recently requested that U.N. peacekeeping
forces be deployed and the whole of Sudan.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.430
Why did you do that?

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:04.449
Why is the U.N. needed now in Sudan?

00:07:04.449 --> 00:07:08.639
Actually let us put this into its proper context.

00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:14.330
We did not just wake up one day and said we
want the U.N. to come to the country.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.259
The U.N. is there, we are not calling it
but for the whole of Sudan?

00:07:18.259 --> 00:07:25.440
The U.N. is there under Chapter 7 meaning
that if there is anything that you could closely

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.229
call it loss of sovereignty, is what is happening
today.

00:07:28.229 --> 00:07:34.240
What we are calling for is to move the U.N.
from Chapter 7 to Chapter 6 which would allow

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:42.620
us to express our wish and if you could call
it anywhere, dictate on the UN on our priorities.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:49.610
This is where we would like to create an opportunity
where we tell the U.N., this is what we want

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:54.940
like you to come do one, two, three, four,
on our terms.

00:07:54.940 --> 00:08:01.389
The whole country approach is an idea we discussed
in our national committee for a number of

00:08:01.389 --> 00:08:02.479
months.

00:08:02.479 --> 00:08:08.669
What it tells us, in the past that the U.N.
intervention in Sudan was compartmentalized;

00:08:08.669 --> 00:08:14.120
it is in Darfur, in Blue Nile, in the Nuba
Mountains, South Kordofan and all that.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:19.750
What would like to see, when we see as a whole
country approach is addressing the challenges

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:25.099
and the issues and the requirement and objectives
of the entire transitional period.

00:08:25.099 --> 00:08:33.050
This certainly has some agenda which is of
national nature of a whole country.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:36.500
When you talk about elections, we will not
just have them in Darfur; it will be the whole

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:37.800
country.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:43.880
A constitutional conference it will engulf
the entire country, the process itself.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:50.470
We would like to enlist the support of the
U.N. in those processes of a national nature

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:54.460
that is why we call it a whole country approach.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:59.770
The support could be providing one adviser
could be providing technical support.

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:02.810
Take an example, the election.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:08.570
Today we would like to embark on a process
that will conclude this transitional period

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:10.460
with an election.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:19.150
The U.N. has accumulated experiences technical
and otherwise across the globe, support on

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:25.360
addressing issues of election systems an election
system that will provide us with an opportunity

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.770
to represent all our people.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:33.970
The U.N could provide that so it's not about
entrusting this entirely to the U.N.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:40.080
The funding of the elections, the U.N. has
accumulated very rich experience in generating

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.430
resources and funds to support the elections.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:47.940
So it is only perfect and we are part of the
U.N., it’s not like another body will rule

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.710
somebody but it's coming from somewhere.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:54.260
let's turn to the topic of the hour the possibility
of former President Ahmed Bashir to appear

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:58.100
before the International Criminal Court.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:02.260
Will he be sent over to The Hague?

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:14.350
The idea of justice needs to be set to the
maximum satisfaction of the victim, is something

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:21.150
that was a well-articulated in the constitutional
transitional period document.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:24.240
We will definitely uphold that.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:27.250
There are four ways of addressing this.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.480
The ICC is one of them.

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:32.690
ICC itself has so many levels.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:38.780
It could be an ICC in Hague could be an ICC
compliant court that is in Sudan or in the

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:45.720
region, transitional justice, issues of truth
and reconciliation, compensation individual

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:46.720
and community.

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:57.610
We are not going to rest until the victims,
those victims to be satisfied that justice

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:02.580
not only being perceived but actually being
served.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.760
And that is how we see it.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:07.510
From what I understand all options are now
open.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:11.100
You still haven't decided whether it be, in
the Hague or in Sudan or in a regional court,

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.230
are all options open?

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:13.320
Yea of course, of course.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:18.560
This is something you know, the announcement
of this was part of our peace negotiations.

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:28.630
And I think this is something, I want to tell
you one thing, any person who committed atrocities,

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:34.631
criminal, financial, will have to be tried
and that is our bottom line.

00:11:34.631 --> 00:11:42.290
We are working on rebuilding our judiciary
system and all that.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:47.960
And we hope to have a credible independent
judicial system, Sudanese.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:51.810
Let's talk about Germany and your visit to
Germany, the past couple of days have been

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.190
quite historic in Sudan Germany relations.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.970
Concretely how can Germany help Sudan in this
phase?

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:05.000
The meeting with the chancellor Excellency
Angela Merkel yesterday provided an opportunity

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:12.621
for us to reflect, discuss in depth our interest
our mutual interests for that matter and we

00:12:12.621 --> 00:12:20.070
agreed on concrete areas that German would
work with us supporting us whether it is the

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:26.390
economy, the energy sector, vocational training,
mining, agriculture seminars.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.690
And we're very delighted.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:35.370
This is signalling a new beginning of this
relationship which has very high promise.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:43.600
And we look forward to this cooperation that
would also allow other partners and friends

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.760
and nations to follow suit, what the German
is doing.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.150
You mentioned the economy, Sudan badly needs
foreign investment.

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:54.180
What are your plans to attract foreign investment
to Sudan?

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:55.620
Your government's plans?

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:57.220
Sudan is a very rich country.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:04.810
We don't want to live on hand outs, we are
so rich in a sense that if we are able to

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:11.250
create the right climate, meaning getting
it right in the legal sphere independent judiciary

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:16.750
system, respect for property rights and all
that, and we are working on this, creating

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:22.890
a one stop shop for investors, creating an
environment where a serious, genuine investors

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:29.560
come work with us pay their taxes and be able
to repatriate whatever profit they make.

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:33.740
And we are creating that environment and we're
very confident we'll get there.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:37.890
Sudan is surrounded by many countries that
have seen change because of popular uprisings

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:41.690
and many of them have descended into chaos.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.880
Is Sudan different?

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.610
Absolutely.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:53.860
Sudan is different in the sense that we are
in this middle, as you mentioned it, whether

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:58.210
you call it the Sahel or centre of Africa.

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:01.230
Sudan’s change is unique in many respects.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.700
It's peaceful.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:06.770
It has great hopes for the entire region.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:14.110
I call it, getting it right in Sudan has a
strategic impact and effect.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:23.440
You can imagine the spill over effect in the
entire region, impact in the north, west,

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.160
south and east.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:31.290
What we would like to see is our friends and
partners working with us in making this a

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:32.410
success story.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:39.330
It has all the right ingredients of making
it as success in this sea of misery and conflict

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:40.670
around us.

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:48.750
That's why it is a unique experiment, unique
in nature and all that, and let us get friends

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:52.170
and partners working with us.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:59.110
The world, and that particular part of the
world is looking for success stories that

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:01.410
were absent for a long period of time.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:04.940
Sudan is giving that hope is giving that opportunity.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:06.680
Let us grab it.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:12.070
Let us work together on it and make it a real
success story that will change the face of

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:17.010
that part of the world.

